What does the ternary operator do? Write the syntax.
Refactor this if-else to a ternary:

String category;
if (balance >= 100000) {
    category = "PREMIUM";
} else {
    category = "STANDARD";
}

back.content:
Syntax: condition ? valueIfTrue : valueIfFalse

Refactored:
String category = (balance >= 100000) ? "PREMIUM" : "STANDARD";

More examples:
int max = (a > b) ? a : b;                    // max of two numbers
String status = (txnAmt > 0) ? "CREDIT" : "DEBIT";  // banking domain

⚠️ Avoid nested ternaries — hard to read:
// BAD:
String tier = (bal>=500000) ? "GOLD" : (bal>=100000) ? "SILVER" : "BRONZE";
// GOOD: Use if-else for 3+ conditions

💡 Best practice: Use ternary ONLY for simple value assignment with exactly 2 outcomes.
Never use for side effects (method calls that do work other than return a value).

