Varargs (variable arguments): allows a method to accept 0 or more arguments of the same type.
Syntax: type... paramName   (must be the LAST parameter)

public static double totalDeposits(String accountId, double... amounts) {
    double total = 0;
    for (double amt : amounts) total += amt;
    System.out.printf("%s: %d txns, Total=%.2f%n", accountId, amounts.length, total);
    return total;
}

// Three ways to call:
totalDeposits("ACC001");                    // 0 amounts → total=0
totalDeposits("ACC002", 5000.0);           // 1 amount
totalDeposits("ACC003", 1000, 2500, 750);  // 3 amounts

// Also: pass an array
double[] arr = {100, 200, 300};
totalDeposits("ACC004", arr);              // array works too!

⚠️ Rule: Only ONE varargs param per method; must be last.

